No... computers are not the unitaskers they once were back in the bad
old days (DOS anyone?).  What is so hard about keeping
notepad/vim/emacs/pico/etc. open in another window?  Adding a text
editor to nethack would unnecessarily bloat the game.  Automatically
taking notes would force a particular syntax on users.  I'll bet there
are non-native-english speakers out there who prefer keeping notes in
their native language.  If you hadn't noticed, nethack isn't I18N
compliant; neither would be an add-on autologger.

Nethack comes from the grand old Unix tradition of "do one thing and
do it well."  Just because it was later ported to Windows doesn't mean
it needs to become bloatware like most other windows software!  There
enough in game mechanism to handle simple note-taking (when you read a
spellbook, on what level your stash is located and the like).  I'd
much rather TDT spend their time fixing existing bugs and devising
new, more devious ways to keep us players from getting our grubbies on
that purty-looking necklace!

